  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 28,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.113,
            0.883,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.4. Four flower beds having sides 2 m long and 1 m wide are dug at the four corners of a garden that is 15 m long and 12 m wide. How much area is now available for laying down a lawn?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.176,
            0.467,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Available area for lawn = 172 sq. m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.23,
            0.883,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.5. Shape A has an area of 18 square units and Shape B has an area of 20 square units. Shape A has a longer perimeter than Shape B. Draw two such shapes satisfying the given conditions.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.292,
            0.763,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Possible dimensions of shape A are 6m and 3m; 2m and 9m; 18m and 1m"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.32,
            0.635,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Corresponding Perimeters =18 m, 22m, 38m respectively"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.347,
            0.775,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Possible dimensions of shape B are 5m and 4m; 10m and 2m; 20m and 1m"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.375,
            0.63,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Corresponding Perimeters =18m, 24m, 42m respectively"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.402,
            0.324,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Given P(A) > P(B)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.429,
            0.856,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We may take P(A) = 22m or 38m and P(B) = 18 m and draw the figures accordingly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.456,
            0.881,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.7. Draw a rectangle of size 12 units × 8 units. Draw another rectangle inside it, without touching the outer rectangle that occupies exactly half the area.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.501,
            0.477,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Area of outer rectangle = 96 sq. units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.528,
            0.476,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of inner rectangle = 48 sq. units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.555,
            0.438,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw the rectangles accordingly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.582,
            0.882,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.8. A square piece of paper is folded in half. The square is then cut into two rectangles along the fold. Regardless of the size of the square, one of the following statements is always true. Which statement is true here?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.645,
            0.736,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a. The area of each rectangle is larger than the area of the square.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.672,
            0.882,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "b. The perimeter of the square is greater than the perimeters of both the rectangles added together.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.72,
            0.882,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "c. The perimeters of both the rectangles added together is always",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { 1 } \\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "times the perimeter of the square.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.77,
            0.882,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "d. The area of the square is always three times as large as the areas of both rectangles added together.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.815,
            0.285,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Only C is true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 19,
